NEW FEATURES:

v1.9 - Small reworking of the IPL codes to make the titlebar highlighting
appear correctly when used in conjunction with JrComm... I don't know which
program is at fault, but I saw from a friend's house that it wasn't coming
through correctly and reworked it until it did.

New to version 1.8 is the ability to define colors for ALL the text
columns, the ability to define whether or not you have column dividers,
highlighting of non-local callers based on their city, state, or country,
titlebar background coloring and more that I can't remember right now...

New to version 1.7 is the highlighting of non-local callers.  You can tell
at a glance if any of the last callers were long distance callers.

New to version 1.5 is the ability to define just how many lines will be
displayed.  You're no longer limited to the predefined 10.  I wouldn't
suggest going much past 15 unless most of your callers are at 14.4k+ or
have lots of patience...  <grin>  Also, the states are now lined up in
their own column to make spotting long distance callers easier.  One
feature I'll probably add next time is highlighting those long distance
callers so it's easy to tell how many you've had.


I'd like to stop and thank a few people who have done just that.  First,
and most of all, I'd like to thank Tom Dietz and Ronald Kushner.  Great
software guys!  It would be possible without you.  Secondly, Janne Siren.
I like your E!-Pager and UpdaText programs!  Keep it up!  Joe Vasher; nice
editor you've written...  too bad it costs 1/3 what I paid for the BBS...
I'm afraid I won't be able to support your effort (I've discontinued use of
your software) because I honestly can't afford it, but it IS a nice editor!
And lastly, the only other person I know (myself not included) that's done
Excelsior!  specific programming, Kennith Brill for his conversion (or,
revival) of CyberMech.  I can give you a lot more of thoses mangled Arexx
doors if you've got some spare time...  <grin>


